{
  "category": "idor",
  "chain_with": [
    "mass_assignment",
    "business_logic",
    "info_disclosure",
    "bfla"
  ],
  "craft_guidance": [
    "1. IDENTIFY ID SHAPE: numeric (auto-increment), UUIDv4 (random), UUIDv1 (timestamp+MAC monotonic), Snowflake (timestamp+worker), base32/base62 (often sequential). Sequential or time-based = walkable.",
    "2. WALK THE SPACE: numeric IDs +1/-1 first; if 200+content delta, IDOR confirmed (Rule 6 — authz, NOT credential brute force). Cap PoC to 3-5 IDs.",
    "3. MULTIPLE ENDPOINTS PER ID: /api/users/N, /api/users/N/orders, /api/orders?user_id=N. Object-level (BOLA) vs function-level (BFLA) are distinct findings.",
    "4. NEGATIVE TESTS: ID = 0, -1, MAX_INT, '0' string, null. Edge handlers leak debug info.",
    "5. INDIRECT IDOR: change non-obvious params (notification_id implies user_id; order_id implies account_id).",
    "6. CROSS-APP REUSE: same ID space across multiple apps in ecosystem (main-app and admin-app share user_id) — test IDs from one app on the other.",
    "7. MASS-ASSIGN OWNERSHIP: PATCH/PUT with `owner_id`/`user_id` → other user. If accepted, attacker takes over the resource (different bug class).",
    "8. ID FORMAT TRANSFORMS: /users/123 vs /users/00123 vs /users/0x7B vs /users/123.json. Some routers normalize differently from auth middleware.",
    "9. UUIDv1 EXPLOIT: UUIDv1 leaks creation time + MAC. Generate adjacent UUIDs by tweaking timestamp.",
    "10. DO NOT EXFIL REAL DATA (Rule 7): demonstrate with 2-3 IDs returning distinct content. Don't dump the table."
  ],
  "contexts": {
    "numeric_id": {
      "description": "IDOR probes for numeric integer identifiers — tests whether changing IDs returns other users data. NOTE: length_diff alone is indicative, not conclusive — paginated content, dynamic ads, or personalized widgets can cause length variance. Always verify semantically (different user data in response) before confirming.",
      "tech_match": [],
      "param_match": [
        "id",
        "uid",
        "user_id",
        "account_id",
        "profile_id",
        "order_id"
      ],
      "probes": [
        {
          "payload": "2",
          "description": "Replace baseline numeric ID with 2 — length diff with same status indicates a different record was returned",
          "matchers": [
            {
              "type": "status",
              "status": [
                200
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "length_diff",
              "min_diff": 200
            },
            {
              "type": "not_word",
              "words": [
                "unauthorized",
                "forbidden",
                "denied",
                "not found"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "severity": "high",
          "confidence_boost": 50,
          "variables": {
            "baseline_value": "1"
          }
        },
        {
          "payload": "0",
          "description": "Replace baseline ID with 0 — may return admin or default account data; requires matching 200 status",
          "matchers": [
            {
              "type": "status",
              "status": [
                200
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "length_diff",
              "min_diff": 200
            },
            {
              "type": "not_word",
              "words": [
                "unauthorized",
                "forbidden",
                "denied"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "severity": "high",
          "confidence_boost": 40,
          "variables": {
            "baseline_value": "1"
          }
        },
        {
          "payload": "-1",
          "description": "Replace baseline ID with -1 — negative ID may bypass authorization checks; requires matching 200 status",
          "matchers": [
            {
              "type": "status",
              "status": [
                200
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "length_diff",
              "min_diff": 200
            },
            {
              "type": "not_word",
              "words": [
                "unauthorized",
                "forbidden",
                "denied"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "severity": "medium",
          "confidence_boost": 35,
          "variables": {
            "baseline_value": "1"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
